  "query_preview": "..\nIssued at 224 PM CDT Sat Oct 17 2026\n\nSunny skies and southerly winds have brought warmer air into the\nregion and warmed readings up into the 60s from the chilly start\nthis morning. A shortwave trough moving through Manitoba off\ninto Ontario will help push a surface trough and cold front down\ninto the region tonight and tomorrow. Weak surface high pressure\nbuild in behind the front and temperatures Sunday night should\nget down into the 30s in many areas, so may have to watch for\nsome spots to get down to the freezing mark as the HREF has\nsome 20 to 40 percent probabilities of that reading in our \nnorth and west. Temperatures will recover quickly and remain\nwell above seasonal values as southwesterly flow aloft gives way\nto zonal flow briefly then a building ridge by mid-week. \nSouthwesterly flow aloft into next Friday and Saturday, with \nmost of the ensemble members showing a trough coming out \nalthough there are of course differences in the exact track of\nthe surface low. ECWMF EFI still showing a signal for above \nnormal temperatures, so any precipitation should remain all \nrain.",
